Error [E0204]: `values` is being changed in this call, so it can't be used again here
  --> builtin_mut_receiver_uses_two_phase_reservation_2.jet:4:25
    |
  4 |     &values.push(values.remove(0, .Slot))
    |                         ^^^^^^
 Why: While something is being changed through the write-access marker `&`, nobody else may be looking at it
 Fix: Pass the write-access marker `&` (`&values`) only once, or copy first with `~values`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0204

Error [E0224]: This call writes `values`, but `values` has no `&` mark
  --> builtin_mut_receiver_uses_two_phase_reservation_2.jet:4:18
    |
  4 |     &values.push(values.remove(0, .Slot))
    |                  ^^^^^^
 Why: The method is declared with `&self`, so the call writes the named place it is called on; the mark sits on that place, the same way `edit(&buf)` and `consume(^text)` mark arguments
 Fix: Write `&values`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0224

Error [E0108]: Argument 1 to `.push()` should be Int (a whole number), not Int?
  --> builtin_mut_receiver_uses_two_phase_reservation_2.jet:4:25
    |
  4 |     &values.push(values.remove(0, .Slot))
    |                         ^^^^^^
 Why: Built-in methods need arguments of the right type
 Fix: Use Int (a whole number) here
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0108
